{"id": "EUVD-2026-104294", "enisaUuid": "7c2c2b60-4893-33be-8e67-09862c46ee62", "description": "rdesktop through 1.9.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in process_bmpcache2() in orders.c that allows malicious RDP servers to crash clients via crafted revision-2 bitmap cache orders. Attackers can send an uncompressed order with large width/height or an underflowing mode nibble and short payload, causing memcpy() reads past the receive buffer and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T17:56:06", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/rdesktop-bitmap-decompress-oob-read", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/issues/436", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/pull/437", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/blob/v1.9.0/orders.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rdesktop-through-1.9.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-process-bmpcache2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112279", "GHSA-3rm3-gwm3-q9hj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "df1c19f8-cf57-3c34-94a7-9836a1c5144f", "product": {"name": "rdesktop", "vendor": {"name": "RDesktop"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "71cf1b2f-8ee7-3fff-8db2-9b96cb67fcfe", "vendor": {"name": "RDesktop"}}], "isExploited": false}